<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Day by day the world goes on,</l><l>Just as it has gone before.</l><l>Millions grasp and clutch at life,</l><l>Wond’ring if there could be more;</l><l>Such was I and would be, yet</l><l>Mercy found me out somehow;</l><l>With what gratefulness I say,</l><l>“I’m in God’s own family now.”</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>How delightful ’tis to know;</l><l>How subjective, real, and sweet</l><l>Is this inward joy of grace</l><l>We experience when we meet;</l><l>Life abundant Jesus gives</l><l>As my full reality;</l><l>Praise You, Lord, it’s really true,</l><l>I’m in Your own family.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>At the closing of this age,</l><l>Just before Your kingdom’s dawn,</l><l>May You gain a people, Lord,</l><l>For Your dwelling place, Your home.</l><l>Since for me You gave Your all,</l><l>Everything I lay aside;</l><l>For Your church my all I’d give,</l><l>That You would be satisfied.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
